# Lean Spec Kit Artifacts

Prefer fewer, shorter planning files. Do not generate optional adjuncts unless the user explicitly asks.

## Required per feature (only these)

```text
specs/<feature>/
  spec.md
  plan.md          # keep lean; avoid repeating the spec
  tasks.md
  validation-report.md   # after Spec Kit triad
  review-report.md       # after implementation + tests only
```

## Do NOT generate (unless user asks)

- `specs/<feature>/quickstart.md`
- `specs/<feature>/out-of-scope-notes.md`
- `specs/<feature>/open-questions.md` — put Open Questions inside `spec.md` / `plan.md` / `validation-report.md` only
- `docs/design/ui-not-applicable.md` — if UI is N/A, one line in the lead-dev handoff is enough
- Full `docs/design/<feature>/*` suite when there is no user-facing UI

## Handoffs (token control)

- Prefer short appends to `.cursor/agent-handoffs/handoff.md` (≤40 lines per handoff).
- Prefer feature-local briefs under `.cursor/agent-handoffs/<feature>-*.md` for long checklists; do not dump full task lists into the global handoff.
- Do not re-read the entire historical `handoff.md` when a feature brief exists — read the brief + last few handoff blocks.
- Periodically archive old handoff content; do not require agents to load the full archive.

## Lean writing

- Do not duplicate BRD / architecture / prior epic text; cite paths and section IDs.
- Label Proposed vs Confirmed; do not invent Confirmed contracts.
- Prefer tables over long prose where possible.
